# Module-wide options, all LANTERN_*.

menu "Lantern"

config LANTERN_ON_USB_POWER
    bool "Light the key LEDs while USB powers this half, dark and unpowered on battery"
    default y
    depends on DT_HAS_LANTERN_RAIL_ENABLED
    depends on GPIO
    help
      On a device with a lantern,rail node (a split half of the Cyboard
      Imprint in canon): while USB powers the device, the LED rail is on and
      ZMK's underglow is on; on battery the underglow is off and the rail is
      off, so the LEDs draw nothing from the battery (src/on_usb_power.c).
      The rail is the node's gpios, the pin ZMK's zmk,ext-power-generic node
      would drive as control-gpios; that node stays disabled in the
      consumer's overlay (the source says why), and a gpio hog may hold the
      pin low from reset until the module takes it.

      Needs CONFIG_ZMK_RGB_UNDERGLOW=y with CONFIG_ZMK_RGB_UNDERGLOW_EXT_POWER=n
      (ZMK's Kconfig.defaults sets it y with the underglow),
      CONFIG_ZMK_RGB_UNDERGLOW_AUTO_OFF_USB=n, CONFIG_ZMK_RGB_UNDERGLOW_AUTO_OFF_IDLE=n
      and CONFIG_ZMK_RGB_UNDERGLOW_ON_START=n, CONFIG_USB_DEVICE_STACK (ZMK's
      default on nRF52840, the split peripheral included) and CONFIG_SETTINGS;
      the source asserts each at build time, so a wrong conf fails the build
      with a message. Default y where the node is present: the node is the
      switch, and a target without one (a dongle) builds none of the module.

config LANTERN_BOOT_LIGHT_MS
    int "Light the key LEDs at boot for this many milliseconds (0 = no boot light)"
    range 0 60000
    default 1000
    depends on LANTERN_ON_USB_POWER
    help
      At boot the rail goes on and the underglow lights for this long from
      its first frame, on USB and on battery alike; then LANTERN_ON_USB_POWER's
      rule applies: on USB the LEDs stay lit, on battery they go dark and the
      rail off. 0: no boot light, the rule applies at once.

config LANTERN_OFF_WHEN_IDLE
    bool "Dark once ZMK's activity state leaves ACTIVE, lit again on activity"
    default y
    depends on LANTERN_ON_USB_POWER
    help
      While USB powers the device, the LEDs go dark and the rail off, as on
      battery, once ZMK turns IDLE: CONFIG_ZMK_IDLE_TIMEOUT ms (ZMK's default
      30000) without a key, sensor or pointing input on this device, each
      split half for itself. The next input lights them again, settle-ms
      after the rail. The boot light is not cut short. The timeout is the
      consumer's line (canon's halves set 300000); a cable plugged into an
      idle device lights nothing until its next input (the source says why).

endmenu
